<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-James Hardie half year profit slumps.</title>
<headline>RTRS-James Hardie half year profit slumps.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     34.3 vs 38.1</p>
<p>    Net					14.7 vs 23.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			6.5 vs 6.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Jame Hardie Industries Ltd is a building products manufacturer.  </p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  loss 20.6 vs loss 20.7</p>
<p>    Sales				   913.9 vs  889.6</p>
<p>    Other income			   68.3 vs  76.0</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			     3.8 vs  6.0</p>
<p>Dividend is fully franked</p>
<p>Pay date January 7, 1997</p>
<p>Reg date December 19</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.8 vs 5.6</p>
<p>    Interest				 28.5 vs 40.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   40.5 vs 36.4</p>
<p>    SEGMENT RESULTS (A$ mln, pre-tax)    1996	     1995</p>
<p>    Building products			  50.8	     50.7</p>
<p>    Plumbing and pipelines	     loss 4.5     profit 1.8</p>
<p>    Building services			  10.0		7.0</p>
<p>    Irrigation			     loss 0.3	 loss 0.3</p>
<p>    Investments			    loss 0.5	 loss 2.4</p>
<p>    Interest				loss 13.1	loss 13.3</p>
<p>GEOGRAPHIC RESULTS (A$ million, pre-tax)</p>
<p>    Australia				     2.9	     21.3</p>
<p>    USA					    29.9	     12.0</p>
<p>    SEGMENT RESULTS (A$ mln, pre-tax)    1996	     1995</p>
<p>    New Zealand				  26.2	     15.5</p>
<p>    Other countries			loss 1.6     profit 2.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Brierley Investments Ltd is the largest shareholder with a 27.23 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
